{
  "judgments": [
    {
      "proposal_id": "P0000",
      "quotes": [
        "The term “applicant” is used hereinafter for the individual whose citizenship and identity is being adjudicated, including for form DS-2060."
      ],
      "rationale": "The source explicitly defines the term 'applicant' for the chapter, including in the context of form DS-2060. The existing claims draft omitted this definition, which was flagged as missing in audit unit urn:rulespec:audit-unit:90aefe8d4af88bb973d37b3da5eb920d7870057ef0c77c15d75cc63d03cafda5. The proposal captures the exact text and correct definition kind without distortion.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "P0001",
      "quotes": [
        "A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5."
      ],
      "rationale": "The source defines a material discrepancy as any name change not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. In the baseline draft, this definition was only cited as context for C0001 rather than being represented as its own claim, resulting in missing unit urn:rulespec:audit-unit:51fcee0859f7a6d05349068c1fe6642a0a7fee127013c92b840d0d593e1baa8e. The proposal accurately models this substantive definition.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "P0002",
      "quotes": [
        "Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C))."
      ],
      "rationale": "The source mandates documenting material discrepancies with one or more specified documents, subject to the married names exception in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C). This requirement was absent from the draft and marked missing under audit unit urn:rulespec:audit-unit:549cab621fcd1eb66c2d012c45524faf948e6662e945a2f8bd43b5d919bbaab0. The proposal faithfully incorporates the rule, modality, scope, and alternatives.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "P0004",
      "quotes": [
        "The applicant generally will need the name change documentation to change the name on her/his ID."
      ],
      "rationale": "The source provides this factual statement explaining why name change documentation is needed and subsequently returned. It was previously omitted from the claims inventory and only referenced as context in C0007, leaving audit unit urn:rulespec:audit-unit:a099f549ab65548eec58cff7667ece9fc0b60f02c36e34496167d32507e13558 missing. The proposed addition captures the statement faithfully.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    }
  ]
}
